OPTIONAL, UNBUILT, NOT REQUIRED for the lomiri-camera-app stack.

Userspace already supplies the front mount angle (camera.conf
mount-angle / hardware.fp6LomiriCamera.secondary.mountAngle), so this patch
only matters for other libcamera users (Snapshot, PipeWire clients) that read
the libcamera Rotation property. The fp6-s5kkd1 driver already calls
v4l2_fwnode_device_parse() + v4l2_ctrl_new_fwnode_properties(), so adding the
DT property is enough to expose V4L2_CID_CAMERA_SENSOR_ROTATION.

Apply ONLY after tools/feature-push/camera-test.sh + the GUI checklist confirm
that 270 shows the front image upright (front-orientation-review/README.txt:
vendor roll 270 is not proved to equal the V4L2 rotation convention). The
preserved-symbol DTB 93bfe406... must then be regenerated through
selfie-fp6-boot-dtb.nix and re-audited; no kernel rebuild is needed.

--- a/nixos-fp6/selfie-fp6/fp6-s5kkd1.dtsi
+++ b/nixos-fp6/selfie-fp6/fp6-s5kkd1.dtsi
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
   pinctrl-names = "default";
   pinctrl-0 = <&kd1_mclk3_default &kd1_reset_default>;
   orientation = <0>;
-  /* Rotation deliberately omitted until vendor HVflip/mount transform review. */
+  rotation = <270>; /* physically confirmed via camera-test.sh (fill in date) */
   port {
    kd1_ep: endpoint {
     remote-endpoint = <&kd1_csiphy3_ep>;
